# CONFIG's Ateryx Pids, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigAteryx.cs.
#
# SoftwareConfig adds ConfigAteryx as "Ateryx Pids" - with Flight Modes and Ateryx Zero Sensors -
# only when the link is open and the firmware is Ateryx (SoftwareConfig.cs:231-237), which is what
# a heartbeat from a MAV_AUTOPILOT_GENERIC fixed wing makes it (MAVLinkInterface.cs:6761-6769). The
# SITL these scripts run against is an ArduPilot copter, so the page cannot be opened here: the
# claim this script checks is the list's condition - connected, with every parameter in, CONFIG
# lists the copter's tuning pages and not ConfigAteryx, and the page is not shown.
#
# The page itself is proved by the unit tests in crates/mp-gui/src/config/ateryx.rs: every
# Designer control at its .resx place, the eight wirings (four buttons, four empty handlers),
# processToScreen's binding of each box the vehicle names, Validated into changes and green,
# Write Params through the retrying set - each set in its own try, "Set NAME Failed", changes
# kept - the flash buttons' airborne checks and Read Flash's question, and, against a scripted
# MAV_AUTOPILOT_GENERIC fixed wing over the real link, the list adding the page and Write Flash's
# PREFLIGHT_STORAGE reaching the vehicle.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-ateryx.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 4
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# Disconnected or connected, only an Ateryx lists the page.
expect config.ateryx.listed false

# CONFIG lists the tuning pages once every parameter is in (SoftwareConfig.cs:148-150), and here
# parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
expect params.held > 1000

click tab-config
expect screen config
expect config.page ConfigSimplePids
expect config.pages ~ ConfigSimplePids
expect config.ateryx.listed false
expect config.ateryx.active false
